<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vimy Ridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vimy Ridge · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vimy Ridge, fought on 9–12 April 1917 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as part of the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arras">Arras</a>, was the first attack in which all four divisions of the Canadian Corps fought together. They captured the heavily fortified ridge at a cost of some 10,600 casualties. The victory became a symbol of Canadian nationhood, commemorated by the Canadian National Vimy Memorial unveiled in 1936.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vimy-ridge.jpg" alt="Battle of Vimy Ridge" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Jack · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richard_Jack-The_Taking_of_Vimy_Ridge_(CWM_19710261-0160).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
